module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicTopology.SimplicialObject.Basic
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Comma.Over.Pullback
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.Over
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Localization.OverPullbackMorphism
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Simplicial.CocontinuousTotalSite

/-!
# The simplicial object in sites attached to a simplicial object of a site

Let `U` be a simplicial object of a site `(C, J)` with fibre products. Each simplicial degree
carries the localized site `C/U_n`, and a simplex map `φ : [m] ⟶ [n]`, with associated
morphism `f_φ : U_n ⟶ U_m` of `C`, gives the localization functor `j = Over.map f_φ` together
with its right adjoint, the base change functor `v_φ = Over.pullback f_φ : C/U_m ⥤ C/U_n`. The
base change functor is continuous and its pullback on sheaves of sets is exact, so it
represents a morphism of sites `C/U_n ⟶ C/U_m`, and the morphism of topoi it induces is the
one induced by `j`. These morphisms of sites are the transition maps of the simplicial object
in sites underlying `C/U`.

The total site `(C/U)_total` has as objects the pairs `(n, V/U_n)` and as morphisms
`(n, V/U_n) ⟶ (m, W/U_m)` the pairs consisting of a simplex map `φ : [m] ⟶ [n]` and a
morphism `V ⟶ W` of `C` over `f_φ`; it is the Grothendieck construction of the simplicial
diagram of localizations and localization functors, and its coverings are the covering families
lying in a single degree. Since `j = Over.map f_φ` is left adjoint to `v_φ`, a morphism of
`(C/U)_total` lying over `φ` is the same thing as a morphism `V ⟶ W ×_{U_m} U_n` over `U_n`,
which is what a morphism of the total site of a simplicial object in sites is; and the
covering families of the two constructions are the same families, being in both cases the
covering families of a single localized degree.

## Main definitions

* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver.slices`: the simplicial object in categories whose degree `n`
  part is the localization `C/U_n` and whose transition functors are the localization functors
  `j`.
* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver.sliceCoverings`: the covering families of `C/U_n`.
* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver.totalTopology`: the topology of the total site
  `(C/U)_total`, generated by the covering families lying in a single degree.
* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver.pullbackCongr`: base change along equal morphisms.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver.isMorphismOfSites_pullbackMap`: base change along `f_φ`
  represents a morphism of sites `C/U_n ⟶ C/U_m`.
* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver.pullbackMapId` and
  `CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver.pullbackMapComp`: the transition morphisms of sites are
  simplicial, the identity simplex map giving the identity and a composite of simplex maps
  giving the composite, in both cases by the canonical isomorphism of chosen fibre products.
* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver.sheafPushforwardIso`: the morphism of topoi attached to the
  transition morphism of sites is the one attached to the localization functor `j`.
* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver.homSigmaEquiv`: a morphism of `(C/U)_total` is a simplex map
  `φ` together with a morphism `j(V) ⟶ W` of `C/U_m`.
* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver.totalHomEquiv`: a morphism of `(C/U)_total` is a simplex map
  `φ` together with a morphism `V ⟶ W ×_{U_m} U_n` over `U_n`, which is a morphism of the
  total site built from the transition morphisms of sites.

## Implementation notes

A simplicial object in sites in the sense of Stacks 09WC is a *strict* functor
`SimplexCategory ⥤ Cat` whose value at `φ` is the continuous functor representing the
transition morphism of sites. Base change functors are not strictly functorial: for
`f : X ⟶ Y` and `g : Y ⟶ Z` the functors `Over.pullback (f ≫ g)` and
`Over.pullback g ⋙ Over.pullback f` send an object `W/Z` to the two chosen fibre products
`W ×_Z X` and `(W ×_Z Y) ×_Y X`, which are canonically isomorphic but not equal. The
simplicial structure in sites is therefore recorded below as the degreewise localized
topologies, the transition morphisms of sites, and the canonical identity and composition
isomorphisms relating them, rather than as a single strictly functorial datum.

The localization functors `j = Over.map f_φ` *are* strictly functorial, by
`CategoryTheory.Over.mapFunctor`, so the simplicial diagram of localizations and localization
functors, and with it the total site `(C/U)_total`, is available as a term.

The comparison of the two total sites is recorded here on morphisms, which is where the
content lies: the objects of both are the pairs `(n, V/U_n)`, and the covering families of
both are the covering families of a single localized degree. The compatibility of the
bijection on morphisms with composition, and hence the comparison as an isomorphism of
categories, is not recorded here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09WL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09WL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09W9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09W9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09WC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09WC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0D6Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D6Z)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace CategoryTheory

namespace SimplicialOver

variable {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
  (U : SimplicialObject C)

/-- The simplicial object in categories underlying `C/U`: its degree `n` part is the
localization `C/U_n`, and the functor attached to a simplex map `φ : [m] ⟶ [n]` is the
localization functor `j = Over.map f_φ : C/U_n ⥤ C/U_m` along `f_φ : U_n ⟶ U_m`. -/
def slices : SimplicialObject Cat.{u, u} :=
  U ⋙ Over.mapFunctor C

/-- The degree `n` part of the simplicial object in categories underlying `C/U` is the
localization `C/U_n`. -/
@[simp]
theorem slices_obj (n : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ) :
    (slices U).obj n = Cat.of (Over (U.obj n)) :=
  rfl

/-- The functor attached to a simplex map by the simplicial object in categories underlying
`C/U` is the localization functor along the corresponding morphism of `U`. -/
@[simp]
theorem slices_map {m n : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ} (α : m ⟶ n) :
    ((slices U).map α).toFunctor = Over.map (U.map α) :=
  rfl

/-- The covering families of the localization `C/U_n`: those whose associated presieve
generates a covering sieve for the localized topology `J/U_n`. -/
def sliceCoverings (n : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ) :
    Covering.{u, u, u} (Over (U.obj n)) → Prop := fun 𝒰 ↦
  Sieve.generate 𝒰.2.presieve₀ ∈ J.over (U.obj n) 𝒰.1

/-- The topology of the total site `(C/U)_total`: it is generated by the covering families
lying in a single simplicial degree, a family of morphisms `(n, V_i/U_n) ⟶ (n, V/U_n)` lying
over the identity of `[n]` being covering exactly when `{V_i ⟶ V}` is covering for the
localized topology `J/U_n`. -/
def totalTopology : GrothendieckTopology (Grothendieck (slices U)) :=
  SimplicialCoverings.totalTopology (slices U) (sliceCoverings J U)

/-- A morphism `(n, V/U_n) ⟶ (m, W/U_m)` of the total site `(C/U)_total` is a simplex map
`φ : [m] ⟶ [n]` together with a morphism `j(V) ⟶ W` of `C/U_m`, where `j` is the localization
functor along `f_φ : U_n ⟶ U_m`. -/
def homSigmaEquiv (A B : Grothendieck (slices U)) :
    (A ⟶ B) ≃ Σ α : A.base ⟶ B.base,
      (((slices U).map α).toFunctor.obj A.fiber ⟶ B.fiber) where
  toFun f := ⟨f.base, f.fiber⟩
  invFun p := ⟨p.1, p.2⟩
  left_inv _ := rfl
  right_inv _ := rfl

variable [HasPullbacks C]

/-- Base change along equal morphisms of `C` is given by the same functor. -/
def pullbackCongr {X Y : C} {f g : X ⟶ Y} (h : f = g) :
    Over.pullback f ≅ Over.pullback g :=
  eqToIso (by subst h; rfl)

/-- **Stacks 09WL part (1).** For a simplex map `φ : [m] ⟶ [n]` the base change functor
`v_φ = Over.pullback f_φ : C/U_m ⥤ C/U_n` along `f_φ : U_n ⟶ U_m` represents a morphism of
sites `C/U_n ⟶ C/U_m` between the localizations of `(C, J)` in the two degrees: it is
continuous and the induced pullback on sheaves of sets is exact.

This is Stacks 09W9 applied to `f_φ`, and it is the datum making the localizations `C/U_n`
into a simplicial object in the category whose objects are sites and whose morphisms are
morphisms of sites. -/
@[stacks 09WL "part (1), each transition is a morphism of sites"]
theorem isMorphismOfSites_pullbackMap {m n : SimplexCategory} (φ : m ⟶ n) :
    (Over.pullback (U.map φ.op)).IsMorphismOfSites
      (J.over (U.obj (op m))) (J.over (U.obj (op n))) :=
  StacksRelocalization.isMorphismOfSites_overPullback J (U.map φ.op)

/-- **Stacks 09WL part (1).** The transition morphism of sites attached to an identity simplex
map is the identity: base change along `f_{𝟙} = 𝟙 U_n` is isomorphic to the identity functor
of `C/U_n`. -/
@[stacks 09WL "part (1), the identity isomorphism"]
def pullbackMapId (n : SimplexCategory) :
    Over.pullback (U.map (𝟙 n).op) ≅ 𝟭 (Over (U.obj (op n))) :=
  pullbackCongr (show U.map (𝟙 n).op = 𝟙 (U.obj (op n)) by simp) ≪≫ Over.pullbackId

/-- **Stacks 09WL part (1).** The transition morphisms of sites are compatible with
composition of simplex maps: base change along `f_{ψ ≫ φ} = f_φ ≫ f_ψ` is isomorphic to base
change along `f_ψ` followed by base change along `f_φ`, by the canonical isomorphism
`W ×_{U_l} U_n ≅ (W ×_{U_l} U_m) ×_{U_m} U_n` of chosen fibre products. -/
@[stacks 09WL "part (1), the composition isomorphism"]
def pullbackMapComp {l m n : SimplexCategory} (ψ : l ⟶ m) (φ : m ⟶ n) :
    Over.pullback (U.map (ψ ≫ φ).op) ≅
      Over.pullback (U.map ψ.op) ⋙ Over.pullback (U.map φ.op) :=
  pullbackCongr (show U.map (ψ ≫ φ).op = U.map φ.op ≫ U.map ψ.op by simp) ≪≫
    Over.pullbackComp (U.map φ.op) (U.map ψ.op)

/-- **Stacks 09WL part (1).** The morphism of topoi `Sh(C/U_n) ⟶ Sh(C/U_m)` attached to the
transition morphism of sites of a simplex map `φ : [m] ⟶ [n]` is the one attached to the
localization functor `j = Over.map f_φ`: the direct image of the cocontinuous functor `j` is
the direct image of the continuous functor `v_φ = Over.pullback f_φ`. -/
@[stacks 09WL "part (1), the transitions induce the localization morphisms of topoi"]
def sheafPushforwardIso {m n : SimplexCategory} (φ : m ⟶ n) :
    (Over.map (U.map φ.op)).sheafPushforwardCocontinuous (Type u)
        (J.over (U.obj (op n))) (J.over (U.obj (op m))) ≅
      (Over.pullback (U.map φ.op)).sheafPushforwardContinuous (Type u)
        (J.over (U.obj (op m))) (J.over (U.obj (op n))) :=
  StacksRelocalization.sheafPushforwardOverMapIso J (U.map φ.op)

/-- A morphism `(n, V/U_n) ⟶ (m, W/U_m)` of the total category of `C/U`, that is a simplex map
`φ : [m] ⟶ [n]` together with a morphism `V ⟶ W` of `C` over `f_φ : U_n ⟶ U_m`, is the same
thing as a simplex map `φ` together with a morphism `V ⟶ W ×_{U_m} U_n` over `U_n`, which is
what a morphism of the total category of a simplicial object in sites is. The bijection is the
adjunction `Over.map f_φ ⊣ Over.pullback f_φ` between the localization functor and the base
change functor.

This is the hom-set half of the argument the source gives for its part (2), and it carries **no
attribute**. Part (2) asserts that the construction of Stacks 09WC reproduces the total site,
which is a comparison of *sites*: it needs this bijection to be compatible with composition,
giving an isomorphism of categories, and it needs the two families of coverings to agree as a
theorem rather than by construction. Neither is proved here, so the tag would overclaim. The
composition compatibility is a mates computation: `CategoryTheory.Over.pullbackComp` is defined
through `CategoryTheory.conjugateIsoEquiv`, so its components do not reduce, and composition in
`CategoryTheory.Grothendieck` carries an `eqToHom` coming from functoriality of `U`. -/
def totalHomEquiv (A B : Grothendieck (slices U)) :
    (A ⟶ B) ≃ Σ α : A.base ⟶ B.base,
      (A.fiber ⟶ (Over.pullback (U.map α)).obj B.fiber) :=
  (homSigmaEquiv U A B).trans
    (Equiv.sigmaCongrRight fun α ↦ (Over.mapPullbackAdj (U.map α)).homEquiv _ _)

/-- The bijection of `CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver.totalHomEquiv` leaves the underlying
simplex map of a morphism unchanged. -/
@[simp]
theorem totalHomEquiv_fst {A B : Grothendieck (slices U)} (f : A ⟶ B) :
    (totalHomEquiv U A B f).1 = f.base :=
  rfl

end SimplicialOver

end CategoryTheory

end
